  "summary": "This paper compares a three-dimensional N-doped Ti3C2Tx aerogel electrode with a pure Ti3C2Tx control electrode. Ti3C2Tx was produced by LiF/HCl mild etching; the aerogel was subsequently formed through thiourea dioxide/ammonia-assisted thermal gelation and freeze-drying. The aerogel is the headline electrode, delivering 438 F g\u22121 at 10 mV s\u22121 in 3 M H2SO4, versus 231 F g\u22121 for pure Ti3C2Tx at the same scan rate. The aerogel has a BET surface area of 108 m2 g\u22121 and a principal BJH pore-size peak near 3.9 nm; thickness, interlayer spacing, and volumetric/areal capacitance were not reported."
